{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfaCbWQZ27mJ1QqTm2Yax","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote 8 test statistics to `iter_4/critique/test_stats/`. I ran each one once on the observed responses: each returns a finite float in about 0.01 s or less, well inside the 5 s per-call limit. I didn't run the posterior-predictive harness; the pipeline does that.\n\nEach statistic targets something the incumbent `lapse_individual_balance_alternation` can't represent. Its only inputs are alternation rate and H/T imbalance, it has no side term, and each person's parameters are drawn independently of one another.\n\n| Statistic | Observed | What it tests |\n|---|---|---|\n| `maxrun_pref_alt_conflict` | 0.544 | Preference for the shorter longest run when the alternation cue doesn't favour it (160 trials). This follows up the streak-aversion finding from iter_3 (p=0.002). |\n| `end_streak_pref_matched_alt` | 0.608 | With alternation rates within 0.15, how often people avoid the sequence that starts or ends with a run of 3 or more. |\n| `periodic_pattern_choice_rate` | 0.673 | How often people choose a visibly repeating block pattern such as HHTTHHTT (perfect alternation excluded). |\n| `high_alt_pref_both_above_half` | 0.595 | Whether the quadratic ideal-point shape fits when both sequences alternate at rate 0.5 or more. |\n| `left_choice_rate` | 0.525 | Side bias, which the model can't produce. It was borderline (p=0.064) against the iter_1 incumbent. |\n| `pair_consensus_fraction` | 0.391 | Share of pairs where at least 85% of responses agree, i.e. whether the model's guessing (lapse) term dilutes consensus too much. |\n| `participant_sd_maxrun_pref` | 0.242 | How much people differ from one another in streak aversion. |\n| `participant_corr_balance_alt_pref` | 0.881 | Correlation across people between the balance and alternation preferences, which the model treats as independent traits. |\n\n**Design limit:** the slice I first wanted, pairs matched on both alternation and balance that differ only in longest run, contains a single pair (40 responses) in this experiment's stimuli. I dropped it and used the conflict slice above instead. A clean test of streak aversion on its own would need stimuli built for it in a later design."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1290,"cache_read_input_tokens":50203,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1290,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a936729a-b50b-4fca-bacc-00d77cfc3a99","uuid":"234304c8-a269-47f9-920e-aea2d41b468c","timestamp":"2026-09-30T19:47:13.661Z","request_id":"req_011CfaCbVxGHer59W3NGmzBb"}
